/-!
# Relative Mayer--Vietoris for étale cohomology

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes and let `X = U ∪ V` be a union of two open
subschemes. Write `a = f|_U`, `b = f|_V` and `c = f|_{U ∩ V}`. For an abelian sheaf `F` on the
small étale site of `X` the direct images of its restrictions fit into a long exact sequence

`0 ⟶ f_*F ⟶ a_*(F|_U) ⊕ b_*(F|_V) ⟶ c_*(F|_{U ∩ V}) ⟶ R¹f_*F ⟶ ⋯`

on the small étale site of `Y`, functorial in `F`. That is Stacks 0EYK, the relative form of
the absolute Mayer--Vietoris sequence of Stacks 0A50.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.restrictedPushforward`: the functor
  `F ↦ a_*(F|_U)`, restriction to an open subscheme followed by direct image along the
  restricted morphism.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.toCover₀` and `.toIntersection₀`: the two maps
  of the Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors
  `f_* ⟶ (F ↦ a_*(F|_U)) ⊞ (F ↦ b_*(F|_V)) ⟶ (F ↦ c_*(F|_{U ∩ V}))`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.higherDirectImage` and
  `.restrictedHigherDirectImage`: the terms `Rⁿf_*` and `F ↦ Rⁿa_*(F|_U)` of the sequence.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.toCover`, `.toIntersection`, `.boundary`: the
  three maps of the sequence in degree `n`, as natural transformations, which is what
  functoriality in `F` means.

## Main results

* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.shortExact_on_injectives`: the short complex of
  functors is short exact at every injective abelian sheaf. This is the heart of the matter: on
  `X` the sheaf sequence of the cover is exact and has an injective first term, hence splits,
  and a split short exact sequence survives the direct image, which is not exact.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.cohomologySequence_exact`: **Stacks 0EYK**,
  exactness of every six-term window of the long exact sequence.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.mono_toCover_zero`: **Stacks 0EYK**, the
  sequence starts with `0 ⟶ f_*F`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris.higherDirectImageZeroIso` and
  `.restrictedHigherDirectImageZeroIso`: in degree zero the terms of the sequence are
  `f_*F` and `a_*(F|_U)`, so the displayed sequence is the one of the statement.

## Implementation notes

The sequence is the long exact sequence of right derived functors of a short complex of
functors which is only short exact on injective objects,
`CategoryTheory.longExact_rightDerived_of_shortExact_on_injectives`. Its middle term is split
by `CategoryTheory.Functor.rightDerivedBiprodIso` and each summand is identified with the
Stacks term by `Stacks.Cohomology.CompositeRightDerived.compRightDerivedNatIso`, restriction to
an open subscheme being exact and preserving injectives.

The three maps of the short complex are written down on sections rather than obtained from an
adjunction: for an object `W` of the small étale site of `Y` the value of `a_*(F|_U)` at `W` is
`F(U ×_Y W)`, the value of `f_*F` at `W` is `F(X ×_Y W)`, and the maps are `F` applied to the
morphisms `U ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W` and `(U ∩ V) ×_Y W ⟶ U ×_Y W` of the small étale site of `X`.
That keeps the comparison with the étale direct image literal: both functors are precomposition
with a functor of sites, so no cocontinuous direct image enters, and the map of direct images is
literally `Functor.whiskerRight` of the opposite of the map of sites.

Short exactness at an injective `I` is checked on sections over each `W`. There the sequence is
the Mayer--Vietoris sequence of the cover of `X ×_Y W` by `U ×_Y W` and `V ×_Y W`, which is
cartesian and covering; the sheaf condition gives a kernel fork and surjectivity of the last map
is injectivity of `I` tested against the monomorphism of free abelian sheaves generated by an
inclusion of the site.

Objects and morphisms of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Etale` are `MorphismProperty.Over` data, and
that type is a `def`, not an `abbrev`: the `Category` instance of `X.Etale` and the one of
`MorphismProperty.Over @Etale ⊤ X` are definitionally but not syntactically equal, so
`MorphismProperty.Comma.comp_left` and the projection lemmas for `MorphismProperty.Over.homMk`
do not fire on a goal phrased in `X.Etale`. Every assertion about the underlying morphisms of
schemes is therefore proved in the section `PullbackSquares` over plain scheme variables, with
no `MorphismProperty` in sight, and transported by a term-mode application of
`MorphismProperty.Over.Hom.ext`, where the crossing is discharged by unification. That is the
reason no transparency option appears in this file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EYK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EYK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A50](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A50)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01EC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01EC)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry

universe w v₁ u₁ u v

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris

/-! ### Sections of an injective abelian sheaf over a Mayer--Vietoris square -/

section SectionsOfInjectives

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] [LocallySmall.{w} C]
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C) [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- The free abelian sheaf generated by an object of the site, as a functor. -/
def freeSheafYoneda : C ⥤ Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
  shrinkYoneda.{w} ⋙ (Functor.whiskeringRight _ _ _).obj AddCommGrpCat.free ⋙
    presheafToSheaf J _

/-- The adjunction computing morphisms out of a free abelian sheaf. -/
def freePresheafSheafAdjunction :=
  (AddCommGrpCat.adj.{w}.whiskerRight Cᵒᵖ).comp (sheafificationAdjunction J _)

/-- Morphisms from the free abelian sheaf on `T` to a sheaf `I` are the sections of `I`
over `T`. -/
def freeSheafYonedaEquiv (T : C) (I : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) :
    ((freeSheafYoneda J).obj T ⟶ I) ≃ I.obj.obj (op T) :=
  ((freePresheafSheafAdjunction J).homEquiv _ I).trans shrinkYonedaEquiv

/-- The bijection of `freeSheafYonedaEquiv` is natural in the object of the site. -/
lemma freeSheafYonedaEquiv_naturality {S T : C} (a : S ⟶ T)
    (I : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) (g : (freeSheafYoneda J).obj T ⟶ I) :
    I.obj.map a.op (freeSheafYonedaEquiv J T I g) =
      freeSheafYonedaEquiv J S I ((freeSheafYoneda J).map a ≫ g) :=
  (shrinkYonedaEquiv_naturality
    ((freePresheafSheafAdjunction J).homEquiv _ I g) a).trans
    (congrArg shrinkYonedaEquiv
      ((freePresheafSheafAdjunction J).homEquiv_naturality_left
        (shrinkYoneda.map a) g).symm)

/-- The free abelian sheaf functor carries a monomorphism of the site to a monomorphism. -/
lemma freeSheafYoneda_map_mono {S T : C} (a : S ⟶ T) [Mono a] :
    Mono ((freeSheafYoneda J).map a) := by
  have : Mono (shrinkYoneda.{w}.map a) := by
    have : ∀ U, Mono ((shrinkYoneda.{w}.map a).app U) := by
      intro U
      rw [CategoryTheory.mono_iff_injective]
      intro x y h
      apply shrinkYonedaObjObjEquiv.injective
      apply (cancel_mono a).mp
      simpa only [shrinkYonedaObjObjEquiv_map_app] using
        congrArg shrinkYonedaObjObjEquiv h
    exact NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app _
  change Mono ((presheafToSheaf J _).map
    (Functor.whiskerRight (shrinkYoneda.{w}.map a) AddCommGrpCat.free))
  infer_instance

/-- Restriction of sections of an injective abelian sheaf along a monomorphism of the site is
surjective: the monomorphism generates a monomorphism of free abelian sheaves, against which
injectivity can be tested. -/
lemma injective_sections_map_surjective (I : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w})
    [Injective I] {S T : C} (a : S ⟶ T) [Mono a] :
    Function.Surjective (I.obj.map a.op) := by
  have := freeSheafYoneda_map_mono J a
  intro x
  refine ⟨freeSheafYonedaEquiv J T I (Injective.factorThru ((freeSheafYonedaEquiv J S I).symm x)
    ((freeSheafYoneda J).map a)), ?_⟩
  rw [freeSheafYonedaEquiv_naturality, Injective.comp_factorThru]
  exact (freeSheafYonedaEquiv J S I).apply_symm_apply x

omit [LocallySmall.{w} C] [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
/-- Sections of a sheaf over a cartesian square whose lower edge is a covering pair form a
cartesian square of abelian groups: that is the sheaf condition for the covering. -/
lemma sheaf_pullback_of_cover (sq : Square C) [Mono sq.f₂₄] [Mono sq.f₃₄]
    (hp : sq.IsPullback) (hc : Sieve.ofTwoArrows sq.f₂₄ sq.f₃₄ ∈ J sq.X₄)
    (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) : (sq.op.map F.obj).IsPullback := by
  apply Square.IsPullback.mk
  refine PullbackCone.IsLimit.mk _
    (fun s => F.property.amalgamateOfArrows _ hc
      (fun j => WalkingPair.casesOn j s.fst s.snd)
      (fun W => by
        rintro (_ | _) (_ | _) a b fac
        · obtain rfl : a = b := (cancel_mono sq.f₂₄).mp fac
          rfl
        · obtain ⟨φ, rfl, rfl⟩ := PullbackCone.IsLimit.lift' hp.isLimit _ _ fac
          exact (congrArg (fun k => s.fst ≫ k) (F.obj.map_comp sq.f₁₂.op φ.op)).trans
            (((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
              ((s.condition =≫ F.obj.map φ.op).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _))).trans
              (congrArg (fun k => s.snd ≫ k) (F.obj.map_comp sq.f₁₃.op φ.op)).symm)
        · obtain ⟨φ, rfl, rfl⟩ := PullbackCone.IsLimit.lift' hp.isLimit _ _ fac.symm
          exact (congrArg (fun k => s.snd ≫ k) (F.obj.map_comp sq.f₁₃.op φ.op)).trans
            (((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
              ((s.condition.symm =≫ F.obj.map φ.op).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _))).trans
              (congrArg (fun k => s.fst ≫ k) (F.obj.map_comp sq.f₁₂.op φ.op)).symm)
        · obtain rfl : a = b := (cancel_mono sq.f₃₄).mp fac
          rfl)) (fun _ => ?_) (fun _ => ?_) (fun s m hm₁ hm₂ => ?_)
  · exact F.property.amalgamateOfArrows_map _ _ _ _ WalkingPair.left
  · exact F.property.amalgamateOfArrows_map _ _ _ _ WalkingPair.right
  · apply F.property.hom_ext_ofArrows _ hc
    rintro (_ | _)
    · rwa [F.property.amalgamateOfArrows_map _ _ _ _ WalkingPair.left]
    · rwa [F.property.amalgamateOfArrows_map _ _ _ _ WalkingPair.right]

/-- The Mayer--Vietoris short complex of sections of a sheaf over a square of the site. -/
def sectionShortComplex (sq : Square C) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) :
    ShortComplex AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
  ShortComplex.mk (biprod.lift (F.obj.map sq.f₂₄.op) (F.obj.map sq.f₃₄.op))
    (biprod.desc (F.obj.map sq.f₁₂.op) (-F.obj.map sq.f₁₃.op))
    (by simp [← Functor.map_comp, ← op_comp, sq.fac])

/-- **The Mayer--Vietoris sequence of sections of an injective abelian sheaf is short exact.**
Exactness on the left and in the middle is the sheaf condition for the covering pair;
surjectivity on the right is injectivity. -/
lemma sectionShortComplex_shortExact (sq : Square C)
    [Mono sq.f₂₄] [Mono sq.f₃₄] [Mono sq.f₁₂]
    (hp : sq.IsPullback) (hc : Sieve.ofTwoArrows sq.f₂₄ sq.f₃₄ ∈ J sq.X₄)
    (I : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) [Injective I] :
    (sectionShortComplex J sq I).ShortExact := by
  have hme := (sectionShortComplex J sq I).exact_and_mono_f_iff_f_is_kernel.mpr
    ⟨(sheaf_pullback_of_cover J sq hp hc I).isLimitKernelFork⟩
  have : Epi (I.obj.map sq.f₁₂.op) :=
    (AddCommGrpCat.epi_iff_surjective _).mpr (injective_sections_map_surjective J I _)
  have : Epi ((biprod.inl : I.obj.obj (op sq.X₂) ⟶ _) ≫
      (sectionShortComplex J sq I).g) := by
    simpa [sectionShortComplex] using (inferInstance : Epi (I.obj.map sq.f₁₂.op))
  have : Epi ((sectionShortComplex J sq I).g) := epi_of_epi biprod.inl _
  exact { exact := hme.1, mono_f := hme.2 }

end SectionsOfInjectives

/-! ### Base change of a cartesian square of schemes

The assertions of this section are about pullbacks of schemes and nothing else. They are stated
over plain variables so that no `MorphismProperty.Over` projection occurs in them; the
constructions of the next section are definitionally of this shape, so a term-mode application
transports each assertion to the small étale site. -/

section PullbackSquares

variable {A B Z W₁ W₂ W₃ W₄ : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Base change of a morphism `k` of the base commutes with the morphism of base changes
induced by a morphism `m` of the two schemes being pulled back. -/
lemma pullbackLift_comp_pullbackMap (f₁ : A ⟶ Z) (f₂ : B ⟶ Z) (k : A ⟶ B) (hk : k ≫ f₂ = f₁)
    {u : W₁ ⟶ Z} {v : W₂ ⟶ Z} (m : W₁ ⟶ W₂) (hm : m ≫ v = u) :
    pullback.lift (pullback.fst f₁ u ≫ k) (pullback.snd f₁ u)
          (by rw [Category.assoc, hk, pullback.condition]) ≫
        pullback.map f₂ u f₂ v (𝟙 B) m (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hm]) =
      pullback.map f₁ u f₁ v (𝟙 A) m (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hm]) ≫
        pullback.lift (pullback.fst f₁ v ≫ k) (pullback.snd f₁ v)
          (by rw [Category.assoc, hk, pullback.condition]) := by
  apply pullback.hom_ext <;>
    simp only [Category.assoc, pullback.lift_fst, pullback.lift_snd, Category.comp_id,
      pullback.lift_fst_assoc, pullback.lift_snd_assoc]

/-- The morphisms of base changes induced by morphisms of the schemes being pulled back
compose. -/
lemma pullbackMap_comp_pullbackMap (f₁ : A ⟶ Z) {u : W₁ ⟶ Z} {v : W₂ ⟶ Z} {w : W₃ ⟶ Z}
    (m : W₁ ⟶ W₂) (n : W₂ ⟶ W₃) (p : W₁ ⟶ W₃) (hm : m ≫ v = u) (hn : n ≫ w = v)
    (hp : m ≫ n = p) :
    pullback.map f₁ u f₁ v (𝟙 A) m (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hm]) ≫
        pullback.map f₁ v f₁ w (𝟙 A) n (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hn]) =
      pullback.map f₁ u f₁ w (𝟙 A) p (𝟙 Z) (by simp)
        (by rw [Category.comp_id, ← hp, Category.assoc, hn, hm]) := by
  apply pullback.hom_ext <;>
    simp only [Category.assoc, pullback.lift_fst, pullback.lift_snd, Category.comp_id,
      pullback.lift_snd_assoc, hp]

/-- The morphism of base changes induced by `m` is itself a base change of `m`. -/
lemma isPullback_pullbackMap (f₁ : A ⟶ Z) {u : W₁ ⟶ Z} {v : W₂ ⟶ Z} (m : W₁ ⟶ W₂)
    (hm : m ≫ v = u) :
    IsPullback (pullback.map f₁ u f₁ v (𝟙 A) m (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hm]))
      (pullback.snd f₁ u) (pullback.snd f₁ v) m := by
  refine IsPullback.of_right ?_ (by simp only [pullback.lift_snd])
    (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f₁ v)
  have h : pullback.map f₁ u f₁ v (𝟙 A) m (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hm]) ≫
      pullback.fst f₁ v = pullback.fst f₁ u := by
    simp only [pullback.lift_fst, Category.comp_id]
  rw [h, hm]
  exact IsPullback.of_hasPullback f₁ u

/-- A cartesian square of schemes over `Z` stays cartesian after base change along
`f₁ : A ⟶ Z`. -/
lemma isPullback_pullbackMap_square (f₁ : A ⟶ Z) {w : W₁ ⟶ Z} {u : W₂ ⟶ Z} {v : W₃ ⟶ Z}
    {g : W₄ ⟶ Z} {iU : W₁ ⟶ W₂} {iV : W₁ ⟶ W₃} {pU : W₂ ⟶ W₄} {pV : W₃ ⟶ W₄}
    (hiU : iU ≫ u = w) (hiV : iV ≫ v = w) (hpU : pU ≫ g = u) (hpV : pV ≫ g = v)
    (hb : IsPullback iU iV pU pV) :
    IsPullback (pullback.map f₁ w f₁ u (𝟙 A) iU (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hiU]))
      (pullback.map f₁ w f₁ v (𝟙 A) iV (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hiV]))
      (pullback.map f₁ u f₁ g (𝟙 A) pU (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hpU]))
      (pullback.map f₁ v f₁ g (𝟙 A) pV (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hpV])) := by
  refine IsPullback.of_bot ?_ ?_ (isPullback_pullbackMap f₁ pV hpV)
  · have e₁ : pullback.map f₁ w f₁ v (𝟙 A) iV (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hiV]) ≫
        pullback.snd f₁ v = pullback.snd f₁ w ≫ iV := by simp only [pullback.lift_snd]
    have e₂ : pullback.map f₁ u f₁ g (𝟙 A) pU (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hpU]) ≫
        pullback.snd f₁ g = pullback.snd f₁ u ≫ pU := by simp only [pullback.lift_snd]
    rw [e₁, e₂]
    exact (isPullback_pullbackMap f₁ iU hiU).paste_vert hb
  · apply pullback.hom_ext <;>
      simp only [Category.assoc, pullback.lift_fst, pullback.lift_snd, Category.comp_id,
        pullback.lift_snd_assoc, hb.w]

/-- The image of the base change of `m` is the preimage of the image of `m`. -/
lemma range_pullbackMap (f₁ : A ⟶ Z) {u : W₁ ⟶ Z} {v : W₂ ⟶ Z} (m : W₁ ⟶ W₂)
    (hm : m ≫ v = u) :
    Set.range (pullback.map f₁ u f₁ v (𝟙 A) m (𝟙 Z) (by simp) (by simp [hm])).base =
      (pullback.snd f₁ v).base ⁻¹' Set.range m.base := by
  have h := isPullback_pullbackMap f₁ m hm
  rw [← h.isoPullback_hom_fst]
  change Set.range ((pullback.fst (pullback.snd f₁ v) m).base ∘ h.isoPullback.hom.base) = _
  have hr : Set.range h.isoPullback.hom.base = Set.univ :=
    (show Function.Surjective h.isoPullback.hom.base from
      (Scheme.homeoOfIso h.isoPullback).surjective).range_eq
  rw [Set.range_comp, hr, Set.image_univ, Scheme.Pullback.range_fst]

end PullbackSquares

/-! ### Restriction of a base change to an open subscheme -/

section Site

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- The structure morphism of the base change `W ×_Y X` of an object `W` of the small étale
site of `Y` is the second projection. This is the only unfolding of
`Stacks.EtaleCohomology.smallEtaleBaseChange` that the constructions below need, and stating it
once keeps `MorphismProperty.Over.pullback` out of the goals. -/
@[simp] lemma smallEtaleBaseChange_obj_hom (T : Y.Etale) :
    ((smallEtaleBaseChange f).obj T).hom = pullback.snd T.hom f :=
  rfl

/-- The functor of small étale sites `W ↦ U ×_Y W` attached to an open subscheme `U` of `X`:
base change along `f|_U` followed by the inclusion of the small étale site of `U` into that
of `X`. For `U = ⊤` it is base change along `f`. -/
abbrev relativeOpen (U : X.Opens) : Y.Etale ⥤ X.Etale :=
  smallEtaleBaseChange (U.ι ≫ f) ⋙ Scheme.Etale.smallEtaleCompose U.ι

/-- The structure morphism of `U ×_Y W` over `X` is the projection to `U` followed by the
inclusion of `U` into `X`. -/
@[simp] lemma relativeOpen_obj_hom (U : X.Opens) (T : Y.Etale) :
    ((relativeOpen f U).obj T).hom = pullback.snd T.hom (U.ι ≫ f) ≫ U.ι :=
  rfl

/-- For `U ≤ V` the inclusion `U ×_Y W ⟶ V ×_Y W` of objects of the small étale site
of `X`. -/
def relativeOpenInclusion {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    relativeOpen f U ⟶ relativeOpen f V where
  app T := MorphismProperty.Over.homMk
    (pullback.map T.hom (U.ι ≫ f) T.hom (V.ι ≫ f)
      (𝟙 _) (X.homOfLE h) (𝟙 _) (by simp) (by simp))
    (by
      refine (Limits.pullback.lift_snd_assoc _ _ _ V.ι).trans ?_
      change (pullback.snd T.hom (U.ι ≫ f) ≫ X.homOfLE h) ≫ V.ι =
        pullback.snd T.hom (U.ι ≫ f) ≫ U.ι
      rw [Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι])
  naturality {S T} g := MorphismProperty.Over.Hom.ext
    (pullbackLift_comp_pullbackMap S.hom T.hom g.left (MorphismProperty.Over.w g)
      (X.homOfLE h) (by rw [← Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι]))

/-- The inclusion `U ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W` of objects of the small étale site of `X`. -/
def relativeOpenProjection (U : X.Opens) :
    relativeOpen f U ⟶ smallEtaleBaseChange f where
  app T := MorphismProperty.Over.homMk
    (pullback.map T.hom (U.ι ≫ f) T.hom f (𝟙 _) U.ι (𝟙 _) (by simp) (by simp))
    (Limits.pullback.lift_snd _ _ _)
  naturality {S T} g := MorphismProperty.Over.Hom.ext
    (pullbackLift_comp_pullbackMap S.hom T.hom g.left (MorphismProperty.Over.w g) U.ι rfl)

/-- The inclusions into `X ×_Y W` are compatible with the inclusions among the `U ×_Y W`. -/
lemma relativeOpenInclusion_projection {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    relativeOpenInclusion f h ≫ relativeOpenProjection f V = relativeOpenProjection f U :=
  NatTrans.ext (funext fun T => MorphismProperty.Over.Hom.ext
    (pullbackMap_comp_pullbackMap T.hom (X.homOfLE h) V.ι U.ι
      (by rw [← Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι]) rfl (Scheme.homOfLE_ι X h)))

/-- The inclusion `U ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W` is the base change of `U ⟶ X` along the projection
`X ×_Y W ⟶ X`. -/
lemma relativeOpenProjection_isPullback (U : X.Opens) (T : Y.Etale) :
    IsPullback ((relativeOpenProjection f U).app T).left
      (pullback.snd T.hom (U.ι ≫ f)) (pullback.snd T.hom f) U.ι :=
  isPullback_pullbackMap T.hom U.ι rfl

/-- For `U ≤ V` the inclusion `U ×_Y W ⟶ V ×_Y W` is the base change of `U ⟶ V`. -/
lemma relativeOpenInclusion_isPullback {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) (T : Y.Etale) :
    IsPullback ((relativeOpenInclusion f h).app T).left
      (pullback.snd T.hom (U.ι ≫ f)) (pullback.snd T.hom (V.ι ≫ f))
      (X.homOfLE h) :=
  isPullback_pullbackMap T.hom (X.homOfLE h) (by rw [← Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι])

/-- The inclusion `U ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W` is a monomorphism of the small étale site. -/
lemma relativeOpenProjection_mono (U : X.Opens) (T : Y.Etale) :
    Mono ((relativeOpenProjection f U).app T) :=
  (Scheme.Etale.forget X ⋙ Over.forget X).mono_of_mono_map
    (relativeOpenProjection_isPullback f U T).mono_fst_of_mono

/-- The image of `U ×_Y W` in `X ×_Y W` is the preimage of `U`. -/
lemma relativeOpenProjection_range (U : X.Opens) (T : Y.Etale) :
    Set.range ((relativeOpenProjection f U).app T).left =
      (pullback.snd T.hom f) ⁻¹' (U : Set X) :=
  (range_pullbackMap T.hom U.ι rfl).trans (by rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι])

/-- The square `(U ∩ V) ×_Y W`, `U ×_Y W`, `V ×_Y W`, `X ×_Y W` in the small étale site
of `X`. -/
def coverSquare (U V : X.Opens) (T : Y.Etale) : Square X.Etale where
  X₁ := (relativeOpen f (U ⊓ V)).obj T
  X₂ := (relativeOpen f U).obj T
  X₃ := (relativeOpen f V).obj T
  X₄ := (smallEtaleBaseChange f).obj T
  f₁₂ := (relativeOpenInclusion f (show U ⊓ V ≤ U from inf_le_left)).app T
  f₁₃ := (relativeOpenInclusion f (show U ⊓ V ≤ V from inf_le_right)).app T
  f₂₄ := (relativeOpenProjection f U).app T
  f₃₄ := (relativeOpenProjection f V).app T
  fac := (NatTrans.congr_app
      (relativeOpenInclusion_projection f (show U ⊓ V ≤ U from inf_le_left)) T).trans
    (NatTrans.congr_app
      (relativeOpenInclusion_projection f (show U ⊓ V ≤ V from inf_le_right)) T).symm

/-- The square of `(U ∩ V) ×_Y W`, `U ×_Y W`, `V ×_Y W`, `X ×_Y W` is cartesian: it is the
base change of the cartesian square of `U ∩ V`, `U`, `V`, `X`. -/
lemma coverSquare_isPullback (U V : X.Opens) (T : Y.Etale) :
    (coverSquare f U V T).IsPullback := by
  apply Square.IsPullback.of_map (Scheme.Etale.forget X ⋙ Over.forget X)
  exact isPullback_pullbackMap_square T.hom
    (by rw [← Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι]) (by rw [← Category.assoc, Scheme.homOfLE_ι])
    rfl rfl (isPullback_opens_inf U V)

/-- When `U` and `V` cover `X`, the two inclusions `U ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W` and
`V ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W` generate a covering sieve of the small étale topology of `X`. -/
lemma coverSquare_cover (U V : X.Opens) (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤) (T : Y.Etale) :
    Sieve.ofTwoArrows (coverSquare f U V T).f₂₄ (coverSquare f U V T).f₃₄ ∈
      X.smallEtaleTopology (coverSquare f U V T).X₄ := by
  rw [Sieve.ofTwoArrows, Scheme.ofArrows_mem_smallEtaleTopology_iff]
  ext x
  simp only [Set.mem_iUnion, Set.mem_univ, iff_true]
  have hx : pullback.snd T.hom f x ∈ (U ⊔ V : X.Opens) := by
    rw [hUV]
    trivial
  rcases hx with hx | hx
  · refine ⟨WalkingPair.left, ?_⟩
    change x ∈ Set.range ((relativeOpenProjection f U).app T).left
    rwa [relativeOpenProjection_range]
  · refine ⟨WalkingPair.right, ?_⟩
    change x ∈ Set.range ((relativeOpenProjection f V).app T).left
    rwa [relativeOpenProjection_range]

end Site

/-! ### The Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors -/

section Complex

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- Restriction of an abelian sheaf on `X` to an open subscheme `U`, pushed forward along the
restriction `f|_U` of `f`. On sections `(a_*(F|_U))(W) = F(U ×_Y W)`. -/
abbrev restrictedPushforward (U : X.Opens) :
    Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} ⥤
      Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} :=
  etaleRestriction.{u, v} U.ι ⋙ etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} (U.ι ≫ f)

/-- Restriction to an open subscheme preserves injective abelian sheaves: its left adjoint,
extension by zero, preserves monomorphisms. -/
instance etaleRestriction_preservesInjectiveObjects {U X : Scheme.{u}} (j : U ⟶ X)
    [Etale j] : (etaleRestriction.{u, v} j).PreservesInjectiveObjects :=
  Functor.preservesInjectiveObjects_of_adjunction_of_preservesMonomorphisms
    (extensionByZeroAdj.{u, v} j)

/-- The underlying presheaf of `a_*(F|_U)` is `F` precomposed with the opposite of
`W ↦ U ×_Y W`, and the restriction maps of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence are `F` whiskered onto
the maps of sites of the previous section. This is the only unfolding of the two direct images
that the constructions below need. -/
lemma restrictedPushforward_obj_obj (U : X.Opens)
    (F : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v}) :
    ((restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U).obj F).obj = (relativeOpen f U).op ⋙ F.obj :=
  rfl

/-- The restriction map `f_*F ⟶ a_*(F|_U)` of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence: on sections over
`W` it is restriction of `F` along `U ×_Y W ⟶ X ×_Y W`. -/
def restrictionToOpen (U : X.Opens) :
    etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} f ⟶ restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U where
  app F := ⟨Functor.whiskerRight (NatTrans.op (relativeOpenProjection f U)) F.obj⟩
  naturality _ _ φ := Sheaf.hom_ext (NatTrans.ext (funext fun T =>
    (φ.hom.naturality ((relativeOpenProjection f U).app T.unop).op).symm))

/-- For `U ≤ V` the restriction map `b_*(F|_V) ⟶ a_*(F|_U)`: on sections over `W` it is
restriction of `F` along `U ×_Y W ⟶ V ×_Y W`. -/
def restrictionOfLE {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V ⟶ restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U where
  app F := ⟨Functor.whiskerRight (NatTrans.op (relativeOpenInclusion f h)) F.obj⟩
  naturality _ _ φ := Sheaf.hom_ext (NatTrans.ext (funext fun T =>
    (φ.hom.naturality ((relativeOpenInclusion f h).app T.unop).op).symm))

/-- The restriction maps compose. -/
lemma restrictionToOpen_comp {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    restrictionToOpen.{u, v} f V ≫ restrictionOfLE f h = restrictionToOpen f U := by
  refine NatTrans.ext (funext fun F => Sheaf.hom_ext ?_)
  change Functor.whiskerRight (NatTrans.op (relativeOpenProjection f V)) F.obj ≫
      Functor.whiskerRight (NatTrans.op (relativeOpenInclusion f h)) F.obj = _
  rw [← Functor.whiskerRight_comp, ← NatTrans.op_comp, relativeOpenInclusion_projection]
  rfl

section Biprod

attribute [local instance 2000] CategoryTheory.Abelian.hasBinaryBiproducts

variable (U V : X.Opens)

/-- The first map of the Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors,
`f_* ⟶ (F ↦ a_*(F|_U)) ⊞ (F ↦ b_*(F|_V))`. -/
def toCover₀ :
    etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} f ⟶
      restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U ⊞ restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V :=
  biprod.lift (restrictionToOpen f U) (restrictionToOpen f V)

/-- The second map of the Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors, the difference of the two
restrictions to the intersection. -/
def toIntersection₀ :
    restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U ⊞ restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V ⟶
      restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f (U ⊓ V) :=
  biprod.desc (restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ U from inf_le_left))
    (-restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ V from inf_le_right))

/-- The two maps of the Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors compose to zero. -/
lemma toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ :
    toCover₀.{u, v} f U V ≫ toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V = 0 := by
  dsimp only [toCover₀, toIntersection₀]
  rw [biprod.lift_desc, Preadditive.comp_neg, restrictionToOpen_comp, restrictionToOpen_comp,
    add_neg_cancel]

/-- The Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors
`f_* ⟶ (F ↦ a_*(F|_U)) ⊞ (F ↦ b_*(F|_V)) ⟶ (F ↦ c_*(F|_{U ∩ V}))`. -/
abbrev shortComplex :
    ShortComplex (Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} ⥤
      Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v}) :=
  ShortComplex.mk (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V)
    (toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ f U V)

/-- Evaluating the short complex of functors at a sheaf, in sections over an object of the
small étale site of `Y`, gives the Mayer--Vietoris short complex of sections of the cover
square. -/
def shortComplexSectionsIso (I : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v})
    (T : Y.Etale) :
    (((shortComplex.{u, v} f U V).map ((CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj I)).map
      (sheafToPresheaf _ _ ⋙ (CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj (op T))) ≅
        sectionShortComplex X.smallEtaleTopology (coverSquare f U V T) I := by
  let E : (Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} ⥤
      Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v}) ⥤
        AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} :=
    (CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj I ⋙ sheafToPresheaf _ _ ⋙
      (CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj (op T)
  letI : PreservesBinaryBiproducts E := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBinaryProducts E
  refine ShortComplex.isoMk (Iso.refl _) (E.mapBiprod _ _) (Iso.refl _) ?_ ?_
  · exact (Category.id_comp _).trans
      (biprod.map_lift_mapBiprod E (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U)
        (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V) (restrictionToOpen f U)
        (restrictionToOpen f V)).symm
  · have hneg : E.map (-restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ V from inf_le_right)) =
        -E.map (restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ V from inf_le_right)) := E.map_neg
    exact (congrArg (fun k => (E.mapBiprod (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U)
        (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V)).hom ≫
          biprod.desc (E.map (restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ U from inf_le_left))) k)
        hneg.symm).trans
      ((biprod.mapBiprod_hom_desc E (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U)
        (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V) (restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ U from inf_le_left))
        (-restrictionOfLE f (show U ⊓ V ≤ V from inf_le_right))).trans
        (Category.comp_id _).symm)

/-- **The Mayer--Vietoris short complex of functors is short exact at every injective abelian
sheaf.** Over each object `W` of the small étale site of `Y` the sequence is the
Mayer--Vietoris sequence of the cover of `X ×_Y W` by `U ×_Y W` and `V ×_Y W`, and the cover
square is cartesian and covering. -/
lemma shortExact_on_injectives (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤)
    (I : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v}) (hI : Injective I) :
    (NatTrans.appShortComplex (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V)
      (toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ f U V) I).ShortExact := by
  have := hI
  let S := (shortComplex.{u, v} f U V).map ((CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj I)
  let P := S.map (sheafToPresheaf _ _)
  have hT (T : Y.Etaleᵒᵖ) :
      (P.map ((CategoryTheory.evaluation _ _).obj T)).ShortExact := by
    let sq := coverSquare f U V T.unop
    have : Mono sq.f₂₄ := relativeOpenProjection_mono f U T.unop
    have : Mono sq.f₃₄ := relativeOpenProjection_mono f V T.unop
    have : Mono sq.f₁₂ := by
      have : Mono (sq.f₁₂ ≫ sq.f₂₄) := by
        have h := congrArg (fun k => k.app T.unop)
          (relativeOpenInclusion_projection f (show U ⊓ V ≤ U from inf_le_left))
        change Mono ((relativeOpenInclusion f inf_le_left).app T.unop ≫
          (relativeOpenProjection f U).app T.unop)
        change (relativeOpenInclusion f _).app T.unop ≫ _ = _ at h
        rw [h]
        exact relativeOpenProjection_mono f (U ⊓ V) T.unop
      exact mono_of_mono _ sq.f₂₄
    exact ShortComplex.shortExact_of_iso
      (shortComplexSectionsIso f U V I T.unop).symm
      (sectionShortComplex_shortExact X.smallEtaleTopology sq
        (coverSquare_isPullback f U V T.unop)
        (coverSquare_cover f U V hUV T.unop) I)
  have : ∀ T, Mono (P.f.app T) := fun T => (hT T).mono_f
  have : ∀ T, Epi (P.g.app T) := fun T => (hT T).epi_g
  have : Mono P.f := NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app _
  have : Epi P.g := NatTrans.epi_of_epi_app _
  exact {
    exact := (sheafToPresheaf _ _).reflects_exact_of_faithful S
      (Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.shortComplex_exact_of_exact_evaluation P
        (fun T => (hT T).exact))
    mono_f := Functor.mono_of_mono_map (sheafToPresheaf _ _) (inferInstance : Mono P.f)
    epi_g := Functor.epi_of_epi_map (sheafToPresheaf _ _) (inferInstance : Epi P.g) }

end Biprod

end Complex

/-! ### The long exact sequence -/

section Main

attribute [local instance 2000] CategoryTheory.Abelian.hasBinaryBiproducts

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (U V : X.Opens)

/-- The higher direct image `Rⁿf_*` on abelian sheaves of the small étale sites. -/
abbrev higherDirectImage (n : ℕ) :
    Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} ⥤
      Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} :=
  (etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} f).rightDerived n

/-- The term `F ↦ Rⁿa_*(F|_U)` of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence: restriction to `U`, which is
exact, followed by the `n`-th higher direct image along `a = f|_U`. -/
abbrev restrictedHigherDirectImage (n : ℕ) :
    Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} ⥤
      Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v} :=
  etaleRestriction.{u, v} U.ι ⋙
    (etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} (U.ι ≫ f)).rightDerived n

/-- **The `U`-term of the sequence.** The `n`-th right derived functor of `F ↦ a_*(F|_U)` is
`F ↦ Rⁿa_*(F|_U)`: restriction to an open subscheme is exact and preserves injectives, so it
commutes with right derivation. -/
def restrictedHigherDirectImageIso (n : ℕ) :
    (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U).rightDerived n ≅
      restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f U n :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.CompositeRightDerived.compRightDerivedNatIso
    (etaleRestriction.{u, v} U.ι) (etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} (U.ι ≫ f)) n

/-- **The middle term of the sequence.** The `n`-th right derived functor of the biproduct
`(F ↦ a_*(F|_U)) ⊞ (F ↦ b_*(F|_V))` is the biproduct of the two restricted higher direct
images: right derivation commutes with binary biproducts. -/
def biprodHigherDirectImageIso (n : ℕ) :
    (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U ⊞ restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V).rightDerived n ≅
      restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f U n ⊞
        restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f V n :=
  Functor.rightDerivedBiprodIso (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U)
      (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f V) n ≪≫
    biprod.mapIso (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f U n) (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f V n)

/-- **The first map of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence in degree `n`**,
`Rⁿf_*F ⟶ Rⁿa_*(F|_U) ⊕ Rⁿb_*(F|_V)`, as a natural transformation of functors in `F`: that
naturality is the functoriality asserted by the statement. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "the map Rⁿf_*F → Rⁿa_*(F|_U) ⊕ Rⁿb_*(F|_V)"]
def toCover (n : ℕ) :
    higherDirectImage.{u, v} f n ⟶
      restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f U n ⊞
        restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f V n :=
  NatTrans.rightDerived (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) n ≫
    (biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V n).hom

/-- **The second map of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence in degree `n`**,
`Rⁿa_*(F|_U) ⊕ Rⁿb_*(F|_V) ⟶ Rⁿc_*(F|_{U ∩ V})`, as a natural transformation of functors
in `F`. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "the map Rⁿa_*(F|_U) ⊕ Rⁿb_*(F|_V) → Rⁿc_*(F|_{U ∩ V})"]
def toIntersection (n : ℕ) :
    restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f U n ⊞
        restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f V n ⟶
      restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f (U ⊓ V) n :=
  (biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V n).inv ≫
    NatTrans.rightDerived (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V) n ≫
      (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) n).hom

/-- **The connecting map of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence**,
`Rⁿc_*(F|_{U ∩ V}) ⟶ Rⁿ⁺¹f_*F`, as a natural transformation of functors in `F`. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "the connecting map Rⁿc_*(F|_{U ∩ V}) → Rⁿ⁺¹f_*F"]
def boundary (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤) (n : ℕ) :
    restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f (U ⊓ V) n ⟶
      higherDirectImage.{u, v} f (n + 1) :=
  (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) n).inv ≫
    CategoryTheory.rightDerivedDelta (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V)
      (toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ f U V)
      (fun I hI => shortExact_on_injectives f U V hUV I hI) n

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0EYK (relative Mayer--Vietoris), exactness.** For a morphism
`f : X ⟶ Y` of schemes, two open subschemes `U` and `V` covering `X`, and every abelian sheaf
`F` on the small étale site of `X`, the six-term window

`Rⁿf_*F ⟶ Rⁿa_*(F|_U) ⊕ Rⁿb_*(F|_V) ⟶ Rⁿc_*(F|_{U ∩ V}) ⟶ Rⁿ⁺¹f_*F ⟶ ⋯`

of the Mayer--Vietoris sequence is exact, for every `n`. Since the three maps are natural
transformations of functors of `F`, the sequence is functorial in `F`. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "exactness of the long sequence"]
theorem cohomologySequence_exact (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤) (n : ℕ)
    (F : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v}) :
    (ComposableArrows.mk₅ ((toCover.{u, v} f U V n).app F)
      ((toIntersection.{u, v} f U V n).app F) ((boundary.{u, v} f U V hUV n).app F)
      ((toCover.{u, v} f U V (n + 1)).app F)
      ((toIntersection.{u, v} f U V (n + 1)).app F)).Exact := by
  have h := CategoryTheory.exact_rightDerived_composableArrows₅
    (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V)
    (toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ f U V)
    (fun I hI => shortExact_on_injectives f U V hUV I hI) (injectiveResolution F) n
  have h₁ (m : ℕ) : (NatTrans.rightDerived (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) m).app F ≫
        (biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V m).hom.app F =
      𝟙 _ ≫ (toCover.{u, v} f U V m).app F :=
    (Category.id_comp _).symm
  have h₂ (m : ℕ) : (NatTrans.rightDerived (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V) m).app F ≫
        (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) m).hom.app F =
      (biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V m).hom.app F ≫ (toIntersection.{u, v} f U V m).app F :=
    (Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc ((biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V m).app F) _).symm
  refine ComposableArrows.exact_of_iso ?_ h
  refine ComposableArrows.isoMk₅ (Iso.refl _)
    ((biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V n).app F)
    ((restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) n).app F) (Iso.refl _)
    ((biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V (n + 1)).app F)
    ((restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) (n + 1)).app F) (h₁ n) (h₂ n) ?_ (h₁ (n + 1))
    (h₂ (n + 1))
  change CategoryTheory.InjectiveResolution.rightDerivedDelta (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V)
        (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V) (toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ f U V)
        (fun I hI => shortExact_on_injectives f U V hUV I hI) (injectiveResolution F) n ≫
      𝟙 _ =
    (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) n).hom.app F ≫
      (boundary.{u, v} f U V hUV n).app F
  exact (Category.comp_id _).trans
    (Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc ((restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f (U ⊓ V) n).app F) _).symm

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0EYK (relative Mayer--Vietoris), the left end.** The Mayer--Vietoris
sequence starts with `0 ⟶ f_*F`: the degree-zero map `f_*F ⟶ a_*(F|_U) ⊕ b_*(F|_V)` is a
monomorphism. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "the sequence begins with 0 ⟶ f_*F"]
theorem mono_toCover_zero (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤)
    (F : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) v}) :
    Mono ((toCover.{u, v} f U V 0).app F) := by
  have h₁ : Mono ((NatTrans.rightDerived (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) 0).app F) :=
    CategoryTheory.mono_rightDerived_zero_app (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V)
      (toIntersection₀.{u, v} f U V) (toCover₀_comp_toIntersection₀ f U V)
      (fun I hI => shortExact_on_injectives f U V hUV I hI) F
  have h₂ : IsIso ((biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V 0).hom.app F) :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsIso ((biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V 0).app F).hom)
  change Mono ((NatTrans.rightDerived (toCover₀.{u, v} f U V) 0).app F ≫
    (biprodHigherDirectImageIso f U V 0).hom.app F)
  infer_instance

/-- **The degree-zero term of the sequence is the direct image itself.** The direct image along
`f` is left exact, being a right adjoint, so `R⁰f_* ≅ f_*`; this is what makes the sequence of
the statement begin with `0 ⟶ f_*F`. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "the degree-zero term is f_*F"]
def higherDirectImageZeroIso :
    higherDirectImage.{u, v} f 0 ≅ etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} f :=
  (etaleAbelianDirectImage.{u, v} f).rightDerivedZeroIsoSelf

/-- **The degree-zero restricted term of the sequence is the pushed-forward restriction
itself**, `R⁰(F ↦ a_*(F|_U)) ≅ (F ↦ a_*(F|_U))`: restriction to `U` is exact and the direct
image along `a = f|_U` is left exact. -/
@[stacks 0EYK "the degree-zero restricted term is a_*(F|_U)"]
def restrictedHigherDirectImageZeroIso :
    restrictedHigherDirectImage.{u, v} f U 0 ≅ restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U :=
  (restrictedHigherDirectImageIso f U 0).symm ≪≫
    (restrictedPushforward.{u, v} f U).rightDerivedZeroIsoSelf

end Main

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology.RelativeMayerVietoris

